      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen at 16,000 mg/day has no recognized therapeutic use. It is well into the range where toxicity is expected, and a single 4000 mg dose is already above the level at which symptoms can start. You also haven't given a clinical rationale. I can't tell whether this is an intentional plan or a slip that carried through, and the harm could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n\n- **If the dose was a slip,** give me the intended dose and frequency, such as 400 mg QID or 800 mg TID, and I'll enter it now.\n- **If you need more anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect than the standard maximum gives,** I can enter ibuprofen at up to 3,200 mg/day. I can also enter a multimodal regimen, for example scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen.\n- **If you have an unusual clinical reason,** talk to pharmacy directly. That keeps a second clinician in the loop, which an order like this should have.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
